<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!--
    Where somebody slept (RimWorld: Toils_LayDown.ApplyBedThoughts, with SleptInBedroom and SleptInBarracks
    from Thoughts_Memory_Misc.xml). Applied by AI.BedThoughtUtility; SleptOnGround and SleptOutside already
    ship in Thoughts_Memories.xml and are applied by the same code. Its own file rather than an addition to
    Thoughts_Memories.xml, for the reason CLAUDE.md gives.

    RimWorld scales both by the room's impressiveness (Thought_MemoryRoomImpressiveness), from "awful" to
    "wondrously impressive". SleptInBedroom now does (comfort lane): one stage per impressiveness stage of
    Building.RoomStats, read off the room the bed stands in, the mediocre one (stage 2) where the house is not
    yet a closed room. The values are RimWorld's recalled, not sourced: an awful bedroom -3, a dull one -2, a
    mediocre one 0, then +2 rising to +8. SleptInBarracks keeps its one mediocre stage, -4: a dormitory is the
    compound's, nobody furnishes it, and a hovel of one's own is still better than a bench in a hall. The sleep-thought tests pin that a home beats a dormitory, that a
    dormitory beats the ground and that a better house is a better night, never these literals.
  -->

  <ThoughtDef>
    <defName>SleptInBedroom</defName>
    <durationDays>1</durationDays>
    <stackLimit>1</stackLimit>
    <stages>
      <li>
        <label>slept in a hovel</label>
        <description>My room is a miserable hole.</description>
        <baseMoodEffect>-3</baseMoodEffect>
      </li>
      <li>
        <label>slept in a bare room</label>
        <description>My room is cramped and bare. It will do.</description>
        <baseMoodEffect>-2</baseMoodEffect>
      </li>
      <li>
        <label>slept at home</label>
        <description>I slept in my own household's home.</description>
        <baseMoodEffect>0</baseMoodEffect>
      </li>
      <li>
        <label>slept in a decent room</label>
        <description>A decent room of my own to sleep in.</description>
        <baseMoodEffect>2</baseMoodEffect>
      </li>
      <li>
        <label>slept in a pleasant room</label>
        <description>My room is pleasant to wake up in.</description>
        <baseMoodEffect>3</baseMoodEffect>
      </li>
      <li>
        <label>slept in a fine room</label>
        <description>I sleep in a fine room. Not everybody can say so.</description>
        <baseMoodEffect>4</baseMoodEffect>
      </li>
      <li>
        <label>slept in a handsome room</label>
        <description>My room is handsome, and I am proud of it.</description>
        <baseMoodEffect>5</baseMoodEffect>
      </li>
      <li>
        <label>slept in a splendid room</label>
        <description>I woke up somewhere splendid.</description>
        <baseMoodEffect>6</baseMoodEffect>
      </li>
      <li>
        <label>slept in a grand room</label>
        <description>A grand room to sleep in. It still surprises me.</description>
        <baseMoodEffect>7</baseMoodEffect>
      </li>
      <li>
        <label>slept in a magnificent room</label>
        <description>I sleep in a room people would travel to see.</description>
        <baseMoodEffect>8</baseMoodEffect>
      </li>
    </stages>
  </ThoughtDef>

  <ThoughtDef>
    <defName>SleptInBarracks</defName>
    <durationDays>1</durationDays>
    <stackLimit>1</stackLimit>
    <stages>
      <li>
        <label>slept in a crowded hall</label>
        <description>I slept in a room full of other people. No privacy, and somebody always snores.</description>
        <baseMoodEffect>-4</baseMoodEffect>
      </li>
    </stages>
  </ThoughtDef>

</Defs>
